Description: Fix heap-based out-of-bounds read in AVI parser
 The avi_parse_input_file function did not properly validate that the
 header data contained enough bytes before reading chunk sizes and
 contents. A specially crafted AVI file with truncated header sub-chunks
 could cause out-of-bounds reads, potentially leading to denial of
 service or information disclosure.
 .
 This fix adds bounds checking before reading chunk data to ensure
 we don't read beyond the allocated header buffer.
Author: deepin-ci-robot <packages@deepin.org>
Origin: vendor
Bug: https://github.com/xiph/theora/issues/24
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1133000
Forwarded: https://github.com/xiph/theora/issues/24
Last-Update: 2026-04-15

